d do nicely  [Music]  it's definitely hot in that spot though  that is a hot spot  the temperature of the wood has  increased  if he had left the rod there longer the  environment still would have become an  issue it's kind of unavoidable but the  lower diffusivity of wood actually made  this possible to see in the short term  it's amazing what you can do with some  scientific thought  if you'd like some more experience with  that today's sponsor brilliant can help  brilliant is an interactive tool for  learning stem that lets you play with  concepts in real time  working with science yourself can really  help make it stick in your memory  if you liked this video you might like  their scientific thinking course where  they have exercises exploring heat flow  amongst other things  but maybe you're looking for something a  little more advanced they also have a  course called differential equations too  where there's a quiz on the heat  equation a major aspect of today's video  brilliant allows you to learn something  new at your own pace or on the go  to get started with a free trial go to  brilliant.org science asylum or click on  the link in the description below  the first 200 of you will get 20 off  brilliant's annual premium subscription  it'll also let brilliant know you heard  about them from me which helps out the  channel  so what would you look at with a thermal  camera i already have a few other ideas  planned for this thing  thanks for liking and sharing this video  a special thanks goes out to my patreon  patrons and youtube members like medic  hertz who's been pledging at the  einsteinium level for over a year and a  half  don't forget to subscribe if you'd like  to keep up with us and until next time  remember it's okay to be a little crazy  did you make this video so you could  justify the camera as a business expense  only partly  no entanglement can't be used to  communicate faster than light when you  measure your half of the entanglement  you immed